    {
      "id": "source-8",
      "type": "review-note",
      "reviewer": "Claude Opus 5.5",
      "reviewedAt": "2026-09-29T03:36:55Z",
      "note": "Target: MainPool 0x4071ee5e created by Neko deployer 0x39fc4cabcccb889934f3952c7a107659abe69949 in 0x26a50904 (9873116:62, ts 1628488047; the creation tx the post-mortem cites). eth_getCode is empty at 9873115 and hashes to 0x2a068f38...375c (21,226 bytes) at 9873116 and 9965526; EIP-1967 implementation and admin slots are zero. The borrow path DELEGATECALLs linked library 0x8c439f25a8c2902d7d13d3d78b858654a2e875ff (validateBorrow, 0x23b6c090) and then calls debtToken.mint(onBehalfOf, amount) (0x40c10f19) and fToken.transferUnderlyingTo(msg.sender, amount) (0x4efecaa5). Every call site is fixed at creation, and neither selector takes the borrower, so no allowance can be checked. MainPool txlist from the deployer through 9965527: creation, 0x944dd5a2 (9873128) and eight initReserve calls. BUSD at 9873395:134 (log 312), then USDT 9873464, BTCB 9873775, USDC 9875084 and others; no later deployer call. eth_call getConfiguration(BUSD) (0xc44b11f7) returns 0 at 9873394 and 0x...0003000a00000000051228a021341d4c at 9873395, 9900000 and 9965526. Age = 1628772811 - 1628488920 = 283,891 s (284,764 s from deployment). Earliest exercise: Etherscan getLogs of all 844 MainPool Borrow logs from creation to block 11000000 (paged by 1,000). The 241 with user != onBehalfOf are 45 by helper 0xfd21385c, created by the same deployer at 9873143, where each transaction sender equals onBehalfOf, and 196 by the attackers, starting with the anchor."
    },
    {
      "id": "source-9",
      "type": "review-note",
      "reviewer": "Claude Opus 5.5",
      "reviewedAt": "2026-09-29T03:36:55Z",
      "note": "Anchor: 0x330bf950 called MainPool.borrow(BUSD, 14,155,776 wei, onBehalfOf 0xbb1a3273ca4776e73af7df4485ba928389c89079) (selector 0x6c665a55) in 0x32a8d8a4 (9965527:96, ts 1628772811, status 1). debug_traceTransaction(callTracer): the debt token 0xc3bc948a is minted to 0xbb1a3273 and fToken 0xdc9cdb40 sends BUSD to 0x330bf950. That is the post-mortem's single direct attack by hacker 1. The account's 103 later borrows go through contract 0xe4ecb6c4, created 2021-08-04 before MainPool existed. The last attacker borrow is 0xdcffa43b (9971112:578, ts 1628789895, 10,000 USDT by 0x52c52cee on behalf of 0x15c3eb91). The loss is the per-asset sum of the 196 attacker Borrow logs listed in source-3, and it equals the post-mortem's totals (BUSD 499423, USDT 3620179, USDC 2792, BTCB 1). The post-mortem says the contract was unverified and that the attackers 'must have access to the code', but it attributes no insider and publishes no finding. Attackers returned about 1.8M USD afterwards."
    }
